# pi-sandbox profile manifest
#
# This file describes one buildable sandbox image profile. Lines beginning with
# '#' and blank lines are ignored. Active settings use KEY=VALUE syntax.
#
# Directives:
#
# PROFILE=name
#   Profile identifier. This is normally generated by pi-sandbox-create and is
#   used to derive the image name pi-sandbox-PROFILE:latest.
#
# BASE_IMAGE=image[:tag]
#   Container base image used for the generated Containerfile.
#   Default: BASE_IMAGE=debian:bookworm-slim. Pi uses a separate private Node
#   runtime under /opt/pi/node; selecting a Node base adds system Node as well.
#
# PI_VERSION=version-or-dist-tag
#   Pi version installed with the official installer and locked release manifests.
#   Releases without official managed-install artifacts fail rather than fall back.
#   Examples: PI_VERSION=1.5.0, PI_VERSION=latest
#
# TOOL=name@version
#   Toolchain to install into the image. Repeatable.
#   Supported tools: go, rust, jvm, uv, fnm, python, caddy, playwright.
#   Node is not a tool directive: Pi's private Node is independent of BASE_IMAGE.
#   Use FNM extensions for project Node versions; no system Node is required.
#   Examples:
#     TOOL=rust@1.90.0
#     TOOL=uv@0.8.9
#     TOOL=python@3.13.7
#     TOOL=fnm@1.39.0
#     TOOL=caddy@2.11.9
#     TOOL=playwright@1.65.0
#   Note: python@VERSION requires a uv@VERSION tool in the same profile.
#   fnm versions may be written with or without the leading "v" release prefix.
#   Playwright installs its CLI, Chromium/Firefox/WebKit browsers with system
#   dependencies, and the independently pinned @playwright/mcp@0.0.84 server.
#   Offline preflight checks tool/extension dependencies; --validate --online
#   also checks supported pinned versions upstream. --check-updates is read-only;
#   --upgrade --patch-only requires confirmation and creates a backup.
#
# EXTENSION=type:spec
#   Additional component/package installed after tools. Repeatable.
#   Supported extension types:
#     rustup:COMPONENT          Example: EXTENSION=rustup:clippy
#     cargo:CRATE[@VERSION]     Example: EXTENSION=cargo:cargo-deny@0.16.1
#     uv:PACKAGE[@VERSION]      Example: EXTENSION=uv:ruff@0.12.9
#     fnm:node@VERSION           Example: EXTENSION=fnm:node@24
#   Note: uv:* requires a uv@VERSION tool; fnm:node@* requires an fnm@VERSION
#   tool in the same profile. FNM project Nodes are installed only in
#   ${XDG_DATA_HOME}/fnm/node-versions/.
#
# NPM=PACKAGE[@VERSION]
#   Global npm command-line package installed into the image. Repeatable.
#   Package names may be scoped. Use an exact version for reproducible images.
#   Examples:
#     NPM=@angular/cli@20.3.9
#     NPM=create-vite@7.1.7
#
# ENV=NAME=VALUE
#   Plain environment variable, baked into the image and passed by the runner.
#   Repeatable. Split at the first '=' after NAME; remaining '=' are preserved.
#   Example: ENV=APP_MODE=development
#
# ENV_SECRET=NAME=PODMAN_SECRET_NAME
#   Runtime-only environment variable sourced from an existing Podman secret.
#   Repeatable. Never put the actual secret value here or in ENV.
#   Example: ENV_SECRET=API_TOKEN=my-api-token
#
# PATH=DIRECTORY
#   Directory prepended to PATH in the image. Repeatable.
#   The value may reference environment variables defined by tools.
#   Example: PATH=${CARGO_HOME}/bin
#
# SHELL_COMMAND=command
#   Trusted one-line shell command executed during the image build as the Pi
#   user. Repeatable. Use APT for root-level Debian package installation.
#   Example: SHELL_COMMAND=go install github.com/sqlc-dev/sqlc/cmd/sqlc@v1.29.0
#
# APT=package
#   Debian package installed during image build. Repeatable.
#   Examples: APT=build-essential, APT=pkg-config, APT=cmake
#
# The generated active profile settings start below.
